# oracle: pair_style meam, single element diamond reference, the w15meam_dia geometry at step 0 only (run 0): pe, pressure and per-atom forces of the displaced 64-atom cell
# oracle: the diamond reference has 4 nearest neighbours at re = 2.165 A, 12 second neighbours at 3.54 A (screened to zero in the perfect crystal) and 12 third neighbours at 4.146 A; the 0.02 A displacements keep every pair distance in [2.0, 4.06] A, so no pair enters the cutoff smoothing window [3.9, 4.0] A (the window form is not verified, see the meam15 report)
# oracle-inputs: w15meam_dia_lib.meam w15meam_dia.meam
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-9 skip=press
# oracle-tolerance: press is not compared here. Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): at step 0 the native press is 1077.289820 bar and the engine's is 1077.290843 bar (9.5e-7 relative), while pe and every per-atom position and force agree to 1e-8 relative; the press difference is in the virial only.
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
lattice         diamond 5.0
region          box block 0 2 0 2 0 2
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 28.09
variable        dx atom 0.02*sin(2.3*x+1.1*y+0.4*z)
variable        dy atom 0.02*cos(1.9*y-0.7*x+0.3*z)
variable        dz atom 0.02*sin(1.3*z+0.8*x-0.5*y)
displace_atoms  all move v_dx v_dy v_dz units box
pair_style      meam
pair_coeff      * * w15meam_dia_lib.meam W w15meam_dia.meam W
timestep        0.001
fix             1 all nve
thermo          10
thermo_style    custom step pe press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             0
